maya: quick eyes on PR #4321 when you have a sec? pushed a fix for the kv allocator rotation bug that could double-free an evicted node under a narrow race. no API changes, internal-only. pinging @kevin @sophia. diff is small, hoping for a quick canary if CI is green.

kevin: thanks for the heads up. quick Q — does this affect compaction ordering or tombstone handling? worried about perf/regressions there.

maya: not touching compaction logic, only the eviction head update path. the bug was a stale `next` pointer used after an unlock. added an assert + comment. snippet: 
```
// avoid using node->next after we release the lock
if (node->pinned) {
  // noop
} else {
  rotate_eviction_head(node);
}
```
added a short unit to cover the stale-rotation case.

sophia: can you add a unit that simulates the interleaving? left an inline about the assert message wording. also please add a changelog bullet under storage.

maya: added test + changelog in the latest commit, pushed branch `fix/kv-rotation-unit` -> `origin/fix/kv-rotation-unit` (git abc1234). test command I ran: `bazel test //storage:kv_allocator_test --test_output=errors` — passes locally.

ci-bot: CI: all checks passed for PR #4321 (bazel, lint, integration). details: https://ci.redwood/internal/4321/123 

omar: quick skim LGTM, one tiny nit on the assert text but not blocking.

kevin: i'll do a deeper pass in the morning, but I'm fine with scheduling a canary if deploy window is open. :+1:

deploy-bot: Canary scheduled: service=runtime-kv, rollout=canary, start=2026-03-17T19:00:00Z, duration=30m. monitor: kv-evictions, memory-usage, rpc-latency.

maya: thanks — i'll merge + kick the canary at the scheduled time if nothing pops. @kevin @sophia if you want me to hold off let me know.

kevin: i'll watch the dashboards during canary and shout if anything suspicious.

maya: awesome, thanks everyone :rocket:
